{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Lest the evil overtake me.</b> When I was among the men of Sodom, the Holy One, blessed be He, would see my deeds and the deeds of the city's people, and I appeared righteous and worthy of being saved. But when I come to be near a righteous man, I am like a wicked man. And so the widow of Zarephath said to Elijah: ״You have come to me to bring my sin to remembrance״ (I Kings 17) — until you came to me, the Holy One, blessed be He, would see my deeds and the deeds of my people, and I was righteous among them; but since you came to me, by the measure of your deeds I am wicked."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:27.920629062Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}